Let a game sign in to Steam before it starts.

Brighter Shores signs its players in with a Steam web API ticket, and the device has no
Steam client to make one. launcher/Pocket (added by this layer) signs in to Steam itself:
with the login it remembers, or by asking for the account and password and Steam Guard.
It then starts the game's Steam session, which the game's Steam library uses through
PocketSteamBridge.h. The launcher asks it first in runNativeGame:, and it comes back to
runNativeGame: when the player is signed in or has chosen to play offline. For other
profiles it does nothing. The Diagnostics menu gains "Sign out of Steam", which forgets
the kept sign-in. Not an upstream candidate as it stands: it names one game's
profile; a general form would read a "steam" section from the profile.

